#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""css-contrast — WCAG contrast, computed, because contrast is arithmetic.

    tools/css-contrast page.html
    tools/css-contrast page.html --min 4.5        the default: WCAG AA body text
    tools/css-contrast page.html --media dark     only the dark colour scheme
    tools/css-contrast page.html --json

Exit 0 when every pair it could compute meets the threshold, 1 when any fails, 2 when it could not
read the file at all.

WHY THIS EXISTS

The harness's own principle is to prefer counting to pattern-matching, and the view guidance
treated appearance as unverifiable. Contrast is not: it is a defined function of two sRGB colours,
and the reviewer who found it put it best —

    Contrast ratios are arithmetic. A small script parsing declared colour pairs would have caught
    defect 1 mechanically.

The defect it was written from: a dark-scheme block overrode `body` and `.card` but not
`.wordmark .ro` (#444444) or the link colour (#0066cc), leaving 1.7:1 and 3.0:1 against #1e1e1e.
Every criterion passed. Nothing in the plan could have seen it, and the page scored 6/6.

WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES

It resolves the cascade the way a browser would, for the subset a self-contained page uses:
tag/class/id selectors and descendant chains, specificity, source order, inline `style` attributes,
inheritance of `color`, and the background of the nearest ancestor that declares one. Colours
in a `@media (prefers-color-scheme: ...)` block are applied on top of the base sheet, which is what
makes the reported defect visible — the failing colour is the one the dark block DID NOT override.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO, and says so on every run

No pseudo-classes or pseudo-elements, no attribute or sibling selectors, no CSS variables, no
`@import`, no external stylesheets, no JavaScript. Anything it cannot parse is listed under "not
checked" rather than passed over, because a gate that silently skips converts absence of evidence
into apparent evidence — which is the failure this whole project is built around avoiding.

The large-text exemption (3:1 at >=24px, or >=18.66px bold) is applied only where the font size is
declared on the element itself or an ancestor. Where it is not, the stricter threshold is used and
the pair is marked, because guessing in the permissive direction is how a gate becomes decoration.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import pathlib
import re
import sys
from html.parser import HTMLParser

# --- colour ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

